# A session adds a tagged test and runs the RFC gate, regenerating nothing.
#
# The five generated RFC files are derived and untracked, so the gate judges the
# summaries, the tags and the audits rather than a committed copy of its own
# output. Until 2026-09-11 this loop reported four files stale and the session
# charged a verification-debt row for each one.
#
# Six markers, one for each step of the loop: the gate answers over a tree that
# holds none of the five, a read of one builds all of them, a read of a shard
# directory that no run finished rebuilds it, the write of a tagged test removes
# them again -- the shard DIRECTORY included, which is the member a file-only
# invalidation could not take -- and the next read rebuilds the shard with the
# new test named in it.

option=timeout:value=180s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture runner/le-rfc-ledger-is-derived
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=rfc-fixture-ready
expect=stdout:contains=gate-judged-the-tree-not-the-pages
expect=stdout:contains=read-materialized-the-family
expect=stdout:contains=unfinished-shard-directory-was-rebuilt
expect=stdout:contains=tagged-test-removed-the-family
expect=stdout:contains=rebuild-bound-the-requirement-to-the-new-test
